Split Group module install from osu_groups install in osu_standard_default_modules().

On Acquia (and intermittently elsewhere), installing osu_groups + osu_groups_basic_group
in a single module_installer::install() call triggers a Group 2.3.x race condition
(drupal.org issue #3391452) where:

  GroupRelationshipType::postSave()
    -> installEnforced()
      -> GroupMembershipPostInstall::installGroupRolesField()
        -> FieldConfig::create()  // fails: "no field_name in values"

The root cause: when Group module's enforced relationships install, the
field.storage.group_relationship.group_roles config has not yet been fully
imported, so FieldConfig::create() is invoked with empty values.

The fix: install group/gnode/group_support_revisions/group_content_menu in
their own module_installer::install() call FIRST, completing all their
post-install hooks (including field storage definition installation) before
osu_groups and osu_groups_basic_group try to define group types and
relationship types.

diff --git a/osu_standard.profile b/osu_standard.profile
--- a/osu_standard.profile
+++ b/osu_standard.profile
@@ -66,8 +66,19 @@ function osu_standard_default_modules(array &$install_state) {
     'osu_library_two_column_25_75',
     'osu_library_two_column_50_50',
   ], TRUE);
-  // Adding these after to satisfy dependencies.
+  // Install Group module and its submodules in their own call before
+  // osu_groups_basic_group. This prevents a Group 2.3.x race condition
+  // (drupal.org #3391452) where GroupMembershipPostInstall::installGroupRolesField()
+  // runs before field.storage.group_relationship.group_roles is fully imported,
+  // causing FieldConfig::create() to fail with "no field_name" on Acquia.
   \Drupal::service('module_installer')->install([
+    'group',
+    'gnode',
+    'group_support_revisions',
+    'group_content_menu',
+  ], TRUE);
+  // Then install OSU group modules and the basic_group type.
+  \Drupal::service('module_installer')->install([
     'osu_groups',
     'osu_groups_basic_group',
   ], TRUE);
